+# Halo V2: fixed coarse batch paths
+
+This is a separate candidate based on `71160fa`, with no performance claim.
+The source-owned setup candidate is independent and is not included here.
+
+Before this attempt, read the existing halo proposal and the actual ELF audit
+recorded in `work/halo-codegen-review.md` outside this checkout. The retained
+`5fe1b5f` library has a 448-byte `coarse_solve_batch` frame; the `71160fa` library
+has a 576-byte frame, unconditional empty pointer-vector headers, and ten halo
+member-load sites in its main function. One MGS active-RHS projection loop also
+reloads the state-array base from the stack where the older binary retains it
+in a register. These are static observations, not measured stall costs.
+
+The initial100 ordinary medians (about16.875s new/off and16.604s new/on versus
+about16.034s old control A) do not establish a code-generation regression. The
+old control B and matching profile work counts were not closed when this
+hypothesis was written. The campaign subsequently retained a strict gauge
+metadata rejection, so these observations are not a newly accepted score.
+Identical outer24/25 iteration counts do not prove identical coarse work.
+
+Hypothesis: one entry dispatch to separate non-inlined member specializations
+can remove halo decisions and unused scratch lifetimes from the reduction-only
+path. `Halo` is a compile-time boolean indicating whether independent RHS halo
+messages are combined. `RHS` means an independent right-hand-side column.
+The shared arithmetic body uses `if constexpr`; the false scratch type contains
+no vector objects. This changes code organization only. It does not introduce
+persistent workspaces, alter matrix layout, tune threads, change tolerances or
+limits, or mix independent GCR histories. GCR means generalized conjugate
+residual; MGS means modified Gram-Schmidt projection.
+
+Argument validation/output resizing, scalar fallback, coarse-thread scope,
+source order, zero-source handling, each projection/update, stopping, restart,
+residual refresh and reconstruction retain their established order. Halo
+statistics exist only in the enabled specialization. The existing collective
+flag validation and default-off configuration remain unchanged. Public C ABI
+and `Impl` data layout are unchanged.
+
+Reuse the existing CTest independent NumPy/operator probes, width1/2/4/12 and
+mixed/zero/tail/fallback/error cases, batch12 MPI2/MPI4, thread-team and overlap
+modes. Make reduction-only CTest environments explicitly set halo0 and add the
+existing runtime-batch script with halo1. No implementation-mirroring test is
+needed. A local x86/WSL run cannot validate Arm SVE or Kunpeng runtime behavior.
+
+Before an Arm performance comparison, require an actual compute-node build and
+check both specialized symbols. The false specialization must have no dynamic
+halo-member load/test or pointer-vector initialization/cleanup from this
+candidate. Inspect its frame and MGS base loads without requiring byte identity
+with `5fe1b5f`; the current object/link layout is retained. Reject an unproven
+static mechanism rather than adding unrelated compiler flags or arithmetic
+changes. Static counts alone do not accept a faster version.
+
+Any performance adoption still requires the same fixture, resources, zero
+initial guesses and complete ordinary12-column samples with matched controls.
+Keep the independent scalar double residual gate at1e-8 and frozen solution
+relative-error gate at1e-6. Instrumented profile timings are diagnostic only.
+Retain the best verified binary and failed attempt evidence. Do not modify the
+active remote source, current campaign, immutable references or old receipts.
+
+Validation results and any blocked conditions are recorded below after the
+isolated implementation and checks, without claiming an Arm result.
+
+Local preparation on2026-11-04 used WSL Ubuntu24.04, GCC14.2.0, CMake and the
+real OpenMPI4.1.6 development libraries. A Release runtime build succeeded;
+23 existing C++ CTests passed. Arm/SVE test binaries ran their available x86
+fallback/skip paths, so this is not Arm instruction validation. `nm` confirms
+two separate non-inlined member specializations. The local x86 dispatch tests
+the halo byte once and tail-jumps to them; the false specialization contains
+no access to that member offset or batch-halo helper calls. These x86 sizes
+and stack frames cannot be compared numerically with the old Arm052 ELF.
+
+Python MPI numerical tests remain blocked locally because NumPy/mpi4py and
+the venv ensurepip component are absent. No packages were installed and no
+fake MPI, lowered tolerance or substitute numerical oracle was used. The
+existing equipped Arm environment must still run those tests, actual Arm
+code-generation gates and physical12-column validation before performance.
+The first separate WSL build invocation could not see its earlier `/tmp`
+configuration directory; a single WSL configure/build/test process succeeded.
+Local command/results/failure logs are retained outside the source checkout
+under `outputs/optimization-20261103/halo-v2-local`.
